# Football Scouting RAG System

## Overview
This project builds a hybrid AI system combining structured football data with Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) to generate scouting insights.

It demonstrates how tabular data can be transformed into natural language analysis using modern ML tools.

---

## Key Features

- Feature engineering from raw match data
- League-aware performance scoring
- Semantic retrieval with FAISS
- LLM-based scouting insights (Phi-3)

---

## Architecture

1. Data aggregation (player-season level)
2. Feature engineering (goals, assists, ratios)
3. League weighting (Premier League > others)
4. Embedding generation (MiniLM)
5. Vector search (FAISS)
6. RAG pipeline with LLM

---

## Example

**Query:**
> Describe the profile of a strong attacking player

**Answer:**
> A strong attacking player is characterized by a high number of goals and assists per game...

---

## Limitations

- Aggregated stats may hide variability
- Limited contextual features (opponents, match importance)
- RAG not suited for ranking tasks alone

---

## Future Improvements

- Player age and potential modeling
- Position-specific evaluation
- Consistency metrics (variance, stability)
- Performance against top teams
- Advanced stats (xG, xA)

---

## Key Insight

> RAG is not sufficient for structured data alone.  
> A hybrid approach combining data processing and LLM reasoning is required.

